<Layouts.app flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user} active={:conditions}>
  <header class="page-head wrap">
    <p class="label">Conditions of sale</p>
    <h1>The terms on which we sell</h1>
    <p class="page-lede">
      By registering to bid you agree to these conditions. They are written to be read; if anything is unclear, ask a specialist before you bid.
    </p>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap legal prose">
    <h2>1. Bidding</h2>
    <p>
      Every bid is a binding offer to buy the lot at that amount, on these conditions. The highest bid accepted when a lot closes, or when the auctioneer's hammer falls, wins the lot, provided it meets the reserve. A bid is accepted only when our system has recorded it; until then it has not been made.
    </p>
    <p>
      In online sales, a maximum bid is an instruction to bid for you, one step at a time, up to that amount. If two bidders leave the same maximum, the one received first leads. A bid in the last two minutes of a lot extends that lot to two minutes after the bid.
    </p>
    <p>
      In live sales, the auctioneer may open a lot below the reserve, may refuse a bid, and decides any dispute at the rostrum. Absentee maximums left before the sale are bid by the auctioneer for you, no higher than needed.
    </p>
    <h2>2. Estimates and reserves</h2>
    <p>
      Estimates are our opinion of the likely hammer price and are not a guarantee. Most lots have a reserve, the confidential minimum the seller will accept, which is never above the low estimate. A lot that does not reach its reserve is not sold.
    </p>
    <h2>3. What you pay</h2>
    <p>
      The buyer pays the hammer price and a buyer's premium of 20% of the hammer price. VAT at 16% is charged on the premium only. Payment is due within seven days of the sale, in Kenya shillings, by bank transfer or at Umber House.
    </p>
    <h2>4. Condition</h2>
    <p>
      Lots are sold as they are. Our condition reports are written with care but are opinions, not warranties; you are welcome to see any lot at a viewing before you bid. If a lot is shown within a year of the sale not to be the work of the artist it is attributed to, we will cancel the sale and refund what you paid.
    </p>
    <h2>5. Collection</h2>
    <p>
      Lots may be collected from Umber House once paid for. We store paid lots free for fourteen days, and can arrange packing and delivery at the buyer's cost.
    </p>
    <h2>6. Your limit</h2>
    <p>
      Each bidder has a bidding limit per lot. We may raise, lower or suspend a limit at any time, and may ask for identification or a deposit before raising it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layouts.app>
